The typesetter tests fetch two SIL Open Font License 1.1 families with
`just fixtures-fonts`. The files land in `/tmp/superreader-fixtures` and are
not committed. They are not linked into the reader or the typesetter binary.

EB Garamond Regular, Italic, Bold, and Bold Italic. Copyright 2017 The EB Garamond Project Authors.
Upstream is octaviopardo/EBGaramond12 commit 106a4a6d377987459ae5e68673a4570f13b957fb.
That repository publishes the font files and has no GitHub Release asset.
The georgd v0.016 tag ships sources only, and its nightly zip is replaced in place.

Noto Serif CJK SC Regular. Upstream is the notofonts/noto-cjk release Serif2.003.

cargo-deny reads Cargo.lock. These fonts are not crates, so the deny allow
list does not include OFL. Putting OFL on that list would allow OFL crates.
The test-only fetch is covered here.

Pdfium is bundled in the macOS app from the bblanchon/pdfium-binaries archive
chromium/8125 (`pdfium-mac-arm64.tgz`). That archive is MIT-licensed. Pdfium
itself is the BSD-licensed Chromium PDF library. The package script copies
`LICENSE` and `licenses/` into `SuperReader.app/Contents/Resources/pdfium/`.
The app does not vendor AGPL or GPL code.

